WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:02.610
- I always like to close out with one last

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.770
feel-good story to bring
you some joy possibly.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.311
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:09.060
(upbeat jingle)
(crowd applauds)

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.380
We've all read the headlines

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.030
about how much these past few years

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.010
have affected kids' mental health

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.800
and that's why I love what one
California teacher is doing

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.470
to support her four- and
five-year-old students.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.350
Each day she does an
emotional check-in with them

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.020
to just gauge where things are with them.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.470
Every day of the week is
different for all of us.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.813
So check out Feelings Fridays.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.243
- All right, really quick,

00:00:33.243 --> 00:00:35.850
I would like to do our Emotion Check-In.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.200
If we're feeling happy today,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.480
you're gonna show me a number one.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.460
If you're maybe feeling
a little bit sad today,

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.510
you'll show me a number two.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.820
You don't have to show
me yet, okay? Hold on.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.510
If you're feeling calm,
remember calm is just content.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.710
I know that's a big
word, just feeling good,

00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:52.700
you're gonna give me a thumbs up.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.440
If you're feeling mad, you're
gonna give me a thumbs down.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.620
So right now, I just want
you to close your eyes,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.650
take a deep breath in
your nose, (inhaling)

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.840
out your mouth, (exhaling)

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.590
and think about how you feel today.

00:01:06.715 --> 00:01:07.558
(audience cheering)

00:01:07.558 --> 00:01:08.737
- I love that!

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:11.580
Let's get this ultra-caring
educator in here

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.800
watching on CW59 in Fresno.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.720
Say hi to Kristin, everybody!
(audience cheering)

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.220
Oh my God, first and foremost,

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.170
thank you so much for being an educator,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.690
it's so important what you're doing.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.020
Thank you so much.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.120
I love, I love, love, love this idea.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.683
How did you come up with this?

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.610
- Two years ago I started
doing it with my kids

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.280
and it was just a quick
like, thumbs up, thumbs down,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.723
how you guys feeling today?

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.450
What I started noticing was that the kids

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.550
really wanted to elaborate and talk more

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.710
about the things that
they've got going on,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.440
but with our busy schedule,
we just didn't have the time.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.948
So what I decided to do this year,

00:01:51.948 --> 00:01:53.790
was have designated, carved-out time

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.230
where they can just talk freely

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.170
about what they've got going on.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:02.943
With these times, it's always
voluntary, I don't force them.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.460
Now they get to be able to elaborate

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.430
and talk about the things that
they've got going on as well.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.401
- Absolutely!
(crowd applauding)

00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:13.770
It's such a healthy exercise
for all of us to do,

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.801
not just our kiddos.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.377
Thank you so much!

00:02:17.377 --> 00:02:19.320
You are such a gift and such a blessing

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.180
with what you're doing in your classroom.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.320
It's so important.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.490
I hope this catches fire,

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.140
I hope a lot of other
teachers clue into this.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.400
It's really, really cool.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.212
I'm liking your posts right
now, all right Kristin?

00:02:29.212 --> 00:02:30.930
(ding)

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.250
All right, and that's not all, girl.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.800
Our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.840
the go-to pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.720
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, ma'am,

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.850
so they're gonna be
writing your school a check

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.946
for $1,000 in your honor.

00:02:43.946 --> 00:02:46.828
(audience cheering)
- Thank you so much!

00:02:46.828 --> 00:02:49.345
I really appreciate it.

00:02:49.345 --> 00:02:51.450
- Absolutely, thank you so much Kristin.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.850
Thank you to all our guests
today, Quinta Brunson,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.970
Sheryl Lee Ralph, Lisa
Ann Walter, Kate Flannery,

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.590
LaToya and Lawrence Zarian.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.180
Y'all have a great day and if it's not,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.637
do an emotion check-in
and try and change it.

